      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think `git_cl.py` is the right place for this. `git cl format`\u0027s main purpose is to shell out to existing formatters (eg clang-format, yapf, rustfmt, etc), and not to contain language-specific custom formatting logic. this CL would also make the tool even more bloated and difficult to maintain. \n\nalso the regex-based approach seems fragile compared to a proper AST parser? eg handling macros/preprocessor directives\n\nideally this could be upstreamed to `clang-format` itself",
